  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of cash, protection and services for refugees and asylum seekers with disabilities in the camps in Dadaab and Kakuma areas.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of cash, protection, and services for refugees and asylum seekers with disabilities in the camps in the Dadaab and Kakuma areas. This UNHCR project provides targeted assistance including the distribution of assistive devices, Outreach activities, community-based rehabilitation, Supports Persons with disabilities (PwD) with shelter construction, and cash transfers. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 8,656 Support to Persons with disabilities, including 1,998 women, 2,292 men, and 4,366 children.</narrative>
  </description>
